            <ArticleTitle>Fatal outcome of homozygous familial hypercholesterolaemia in a black patient. A case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>588-90</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A black patient with homozygous familial hypercholesterolaemia associated with ischaemic heart disease and a fatal outcome is described. The appearances of the coronary artery and aortic lesions on histological examination at autopsy were identical to those of typical atherosclerosis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
